DESC Specifies the number of CXRAs in CPAG121 Constraint: May use pag_tgtid2 through pag_tgtid3 of por_hnf_cml_port_aggr_grp_reg0 when POR_RNSAM_FLEX_TGTID_EN_PARAM = 0 3'b000: 1 port used 3'b001: 2 ports used 3'b010: 4 ports used 3'b011: 8 ports used 3'b100: 16 ports used 3'b101: 32 ports used 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved
F 0 3 num_cxg_pag20
DESC Specifies the number of CXRAs in CPAG20 Constraint: May use pag_tgtid0 through pag_tgtid7 of por_hnf_cml_port_aggr_grp_reg[0,1] when POR_RNSAM_FLEX_TGTID_EN_PARAM = 0 3'b000: 1 port used 3'b001: 2 ports used 3'b010: 4 ports used 3'b011: 8 ports used 3'b100: 16 ports used 3'b101: 32 ports used 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved
R 0x6228 64 - S por_hnf_cml_port_aggr_ctrl_reg5
RESET 0x0 0x7007007007007
DESC Configures the CCIX port aggregation port groups
SGO por_hnf_secure_register_groups_override.sam_control
F 48 3 num_cxg_pag29
DESC Specifies the number of CXRAs in CPAG429 Constraint: May use pag_tgtid8 through pag_tgtid9 of por_hnf_cml_port_aggr_grp_reg1 when POR_RNSAM_FLEX_TGTID_EN_PARAM = 0 3'b000: 1 port used 3'b001: 2 ports used 3'b010: 4 ports used 3'b011: 8 ports used 3'b100: 16 ports used 3'b101: 32 ports used 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved
F 36 3 num_cxg_pag28
DESC Specifies the number of CXRAs in CPAG328 Constraint: May use pag_tgtid6 through pag_tgtid7 of por_hnf_cml_port_aggr_grp_reg1 when POR_RNSAM_FLEX_TGTID_EN_PARAM = 0 3'b000: 1 port used 3'b001: 2 ports used 3'b010: 4 ports used 3'b011: 8 ports used 3'b100: 16 ports used 3'b101: 32 ports used 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved
F 24 3 num_cxg_pag27
DESC Specifies the number of CXRAs in CPAG227 Constraint: May use pag_tgtid4 through pag_tgtid7 of por_hnf_cml_port_aggr_grp_reg[0,1] when POR_RNSAM_FLEX_TGTID_EN_PARAM = 0 3'b000: 1 port used 3'b001: 2 ports used 3'b010: 4 ports used 3'b011: 8 ports used 3'b100: 16 ports used 3'b101: 32 ports used 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved
F 12 3 num_cxg_pag26
DESC Specifies the number of CXRAs in CPAG126 Constraint: May use pag_tgtid2 through pag_tgtid3 of por_hnf_cml_port_aggr_grp_reg0 when POR_RNSAM_FLEX_TGTID_EN_PARAM = 0 3'b000: 1 port used 3'b001: 2 ports used 3'b010: 4 ports used 3'b011: 8 ports used 3'b100: 16 ports used 3'b101: 32 ports used 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved
F 0 3 num_cxg_pag25
DESC Specifies the number of CXRAs in CPAG25 Constraint: May use pag_tgtid0 through pag_tgtid7 of por_hnf_cml_port_aggr_grp_reg[0,1] when POR_RNSAM_FLEX_TGTID_EN_PARAM = 0 3'b000: 1 port used 3'b001: 2 ports used 3'b010: 4 ports used 3'b011: 8 ports used 3'b100: 16 ports used 3'b101: 32 ports used 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved
R 0x6230 64 - S por_hnf_cml_port_aggr_ctrl_reg6
RESET 0x0 0x7007007007007
DESC Configures the CCIX port aggregation port groups
SGO por_hnf_secure_register_groups_override.sam_control
F 48 3 num_cxg_pag34
DESC Specifies the number of CXRAs in CPAG434 Constraint: May use pag_tgtid8 through pag_tgtid9 of por_hnf_cml_port_aggr_grp_reg1 when POR_RNSAM_FLEX_TGTID_EN_PARAM = 0 3'b000: 1 port used 3'b001: 2 ports used 3'b010: 4 ports used 3'b011: 8 ports used 3'b100: 16 ports used 3'b101: 32 ports used 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved
F 36 3 num_cxg_pag33
DESC Specifies the number of CXRAs in CPAG333 Constraint: May use pag_tgtid6 through pag_tgtid7 of por_hnf_cml_port_aggr_grp_reg1 when POR_RNSAM_FLEX_TGTID_EN_PARAM = 0 3'b000: 1 port used 3'b001: 2 ports used 3'b010: 4 ports used 3'b011: 8 ports used 3'b100: 16 ports used 3'b101: 32 ports used 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved
F 24 3 num_cxg_pag32
DESC Specifies the number of CXRAs in CPAG232 Constraint: May use pag_tgtid4 through pag_tgtid7 of por_hnf_cml_port_aggr_grp_reg[0,1] when POR_RNSAM_FLEX_TGTID_EN_PARAM = 0 3'b000: 1 port used 3'b001: 2 ports used 3'b010: 4 ports used 3'b011: 8 ports used 3'b100: 16 ports used 3'b101: 32 ports used 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved
F 12 3 num_cxg_pag31
DESC Specifies the number of CXRAs in CPAG131 Constraint: May use pag_tgtid2 through pag_tgtid3 of por_hnf_cml_port_aggr_grp_reg0 when POR_RNSAM_FLEX_TGTID_EN_PARAM = 0 3'b000: 1 port used 3'b001: 2 ports used 3'b010: 4 ports used 3'b011: 8 ports used 3'b100: 16 ports used 3'b101: 32 ports used 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved
F 0 3 num_cxg_pag30
DESC Specifies the number of CXRAs in CPAG30 Constraint: May use pag_tgtid0 through pag_tgtid7 of por_hnf_cml_port_aggr_grp_reg[0,1] when POR_RNSAM_FLEX_TGTID_EN_PARAM = 0 3'b000: 1 port used 3'b001: 2 ports used 3'b010: 4 ports used 3'b011: 8 ports used 3'b100: 16 ports used 3'b101: 32 ports used 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved
ENDGROUP
GROUP por_hnf_mpam_ns_registers
BASE 0x0
RANGE 0x10000
R 0x0 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_ns_node_info
RESET 0x9 0xffffffffffff
DESC Provides component identification information.
F 0 16 node_type
DESC CMN-600 node type identifier
F 16 16 node_id
DESC Component node ID
PAR NODEID_PARAM
F 32 16 logical_id
DESC Component logical ID
PAR LOGICALID_PARAM
R 0x80 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_ns_child_info
RESET 0x0 0xffffffff
DESC Provides component child identification information.
F 0 16 child_count
DESC Number of child nodes; used in discovery process
F 16 16 child_ptr_offset
DESC Starting register offset which contains pointers to the child nodes
R 0x1000 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_idr
RESET 0x1000f 0xefffffff
DESC MPAM features ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_mpam_partid_max
DESC Maximum value of non-secure PARTID supported by this HN-F
PAR HNF_MPAM_NS_PARTID_PARAM
F 16 8 hnf_mpam_pmg_max
DESC Maximum value of non-secure PMG supported by this HN-F
PAR HNF_MPAM_NS_PMG_PARAM
F 24 1 hnf_mpam_has_ccap_part
DESC 0: MPAM cache maximum capacity partitioning is not supported 1: MPAM cache maximum capacity partitioning is supported
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_CCAP_PART_PARAM
F 25 1 hnf_mpam_has_cpor_part
DESC 0: MPAM cache portion partitioning is not supported 1: MPAM cache portion partitioning is supported
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_CPOR_PART_PARAM
F 26 1 hnf_mpam_has_mbw_part
DESC 0: MPAM memory bandwidth partitioning is not supported 1: MPAM memory bandwidth partitioning is supported
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_MBW_PART_PARAM
F 27 1 hnf_mpam_has_pri_part
DESC 0: MPAM priority partitioning is not supported 1: MPAM priority partitioning is supported
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_PRI_PART_PARAM
F 29 1 hnf_mpam_has_impl_idr
DESC 0: MPAM implementation specific partitioning features not supported 1: MPAM implementation specific partitioning features supported
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_IMPL_IDR_PARAM
F 30 1 hnf_mpam_has_msmon
DESC 0: MPAM performance monitoring is not supported 1: MPAM performance monitoring is supported
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_MSMON_PARAM
F 31 1 hnf_mpam_has_partid_nrw
DESC 0: HN-F does not support MPAM PARTID Narrowing 1: HN-F supports MPAM PARTID Narrowing
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_PARTID_NRW_PARAM
R 0x1018 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_iidr
RESET 0x43b 0xffffffff
DESC MPAM Implementation ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 12 hnf_mpam_iidr_implementer
DESC Implementation defined value identifying company that implemented MPAM memory system component
F 12 4 hnf_mpam_iidr_revision
DESC Implementation defined value identifying minor revision of the product
F 16 4 hnf_mpam_iidr_variant
DESC Implementation defined value identifying major revision of the product
F 20 12 hnf_mpam_iidr_productid
DESC Implementation defined value identifying MPAM memory system component
R 0x1020 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_aidr
RESET 0x10 0xff
DESC MPAM architecture ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 4 hnf_mpam_aidr_arch_minor_rev
DESC Minor revision of the MPAM architecture that this memory system component implements
F 4 4 hnf_mpam_aidr_arch_major_rev
DESC Major revision of the MPAM architecture that this memory system component implements
R 0x1028 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_impl_idr
RESET 0x0 0xffffffff
DESC MPAM Implementation defined partitioning feature ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 32 hnf_mpam_impl_idr
DESC Implementation defined partitioning features.
R 0x1030 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_cpor_idr
RESET 0x10 0xffff
DESC MPAM cache portion partitioning ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_mpam_cpor_idr_cpbm_wd
DESC Number of bits in the cache portion partitioning bit map of this device.
PAR HNF_MPAM_CPBM_WD_PARAM
R 0x1038 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_ccap_idr
RESET 0x7 0x3f
DESC MPAM cache capacity partitioning ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 6 hnf_mpam_ccap_idr_cmax_wd
DESC Number of fractional bits implemented in the cache capacity partitioning.
PAR HNF_MPAM_CMAX_WD_PARAM
R 0x1040 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_mbw_idr
RESET 0x0 0x1fff7c3f
DESC MPAM Memory Bandwidth partitioning ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 6 hnf_mpam_mbw_idr_bwa_wd
DESC Number of implemented bits in bandwidth allocation fields: MIN, MAX, and STRIDE. Value must be between 1 to 16
F 10 1 hnf_mpam_mbw_idr_has_min
DESC 0: There is no minimum memory bandwidth control and no MPAMCFG_MBW_MIN register 1: MPAMCFG_MBW_MIN register exists and minimum memory bandwidth allocation scheme is supported.
F 11 1 hnf_mpam_mbw_idr_has_max
DESC 0: There is no maximum memory bandwidth control and no MPAMCFG_MBW_MAX register 1: MPAMCFG_MBW_MAX register exists and maximum memory bandwidth allocation scheme is supported.
F 12 1 hnf_mpam_mbw_idr_has_pbm
DESC 0: There is no memory bandwidth portion control and no MPAMCFG_MBW_PBM register 1: MPAMCFG_MBW_PBM register exists and memory bandwidth portion allocation scheme is supported.
F 13 1 hnf_mpam_mbw_idr_has_prop
DESC 0: There is no memory bandwidth proportional stride control and no MPAMCFG_MBW_PROP register 1: MPAMCFG_MBW_PROP register exists and memory bandwidth proportional stride memory bandwidth allocation scheme is supported.
F 14 1 hnf_mpam_mbw_idr_windwr
DESC 0: The bandwidth accounting period should be read from MPAMCFG_MBW_WINDWR register, which might be fixed. 1: The bandwidth accounting width is readable and writable per partition in MPAMCFG_MBW_WINDWR register.
F 16 13 hnf_mpam_mbw_idr_bwpbm_wd
DESC Number of bits indication portions in MPAMCFG_MBW_PBM register.
R 0x1048 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_pri_idr
RESET 0x0 0x3f303f3
DESC MPAM Priority partitioning ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 1 hnf_mpam_pri_idr_has_intpri
DESC 0: This memory system component supports priority, but doesn't have an internal priority field in MPAMCFG_PRI. 1: This memory system component supports internal priority and has an INTPRI field.
F 1 1 hnf_mpam_pri_idr_intpri_0_is_low
DESC 0: In the INTPRI field, a value of 0 means highest priority. 1: In the INTPRI field, a value of 0 means lowest priority.
F 4 6 hnf_mpam_pri_idr_intpri_wd
DESC Number of bits in the internal priority field (INTPRI) in MPAMCFG_PRI.
F 16 1 hnf_mpam_pri_idr_has_dspri
DESC 0: This memory system component supports priority, but doesn't have a downstream priority (DSPRI) field in MPAMCFG_PRI. 1: This memory system component supports downstream priority and has an DSPRI field.
F 17 1 hnf_mpam_pri_idr_has_dspri_0_is_low
DESC 0: In the DSPRI field, a value of 0 means highest priority. 1: In the DSPRI field, a value of 0 means lowest priority.
F 20 6 hnf_mpam_pri_idr_dspri_wd
DESC Number of bits in downstream priority field (DSPRI) in MPAMCFG_PRI.
R 0x1050 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_partid_nrw_idr
RESET 0x0 0xffff
DESC MPAM PARTID narrowing ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_mpam_partid_nrw_idr_intpartid_max
DESC This field indicates the largest intPARTID supported in this component.
R 0x1080 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_msmon_idr
RESET 0x80000000 0x80030000
DESC MPAM performance monitoring ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 16 1 hnf_mpam_msmon_csu
DESC This component has a performance monitor for Cache Storage Usage by PARTID and PMG.
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_MSMON_CSU_PARAM
F 17 1 hnf_mpam_msmon_mbwu
DESC This component has a performance monitor for Memory Bandwidth Usage by PARTID and PMG.
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_MSMON_MBWU_PARAM
F 31 1 hnf_mpam_msmon_has_local_capt_evnt
DESC Has the local capture event generator and the MSMON_CAPT_EVNT register.
R 0x1088 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_csumon_idr
RESET 0x80000004 0x8000ffff
DESC MPAM cache storage usage monitor ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_mpam_csumon_num_mon
DESC The number of CSU monitoring counters implemented in this component.
PAR HNF_MPAM_NUM_CSUMON_PARAM
F 31 1 hnf_mpam_csumon_has_capture
DESC 0: MSMON_CSU_CAPTURE is not implemented and there is no support for capture events in this component's CSU monitor feature. 1: This component's CSU monitor feature has an MSMON_CSU_CAPTURE register for every MSMON_CSU and supports the capture event behaviour.
R 0x1090 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_mbwumon_idr
RESET 0x0 0x8000ffff
DESC MPAM memory bandwidth usage monitor ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_mpam_mbwumon_num_mon
DESC The number of MBWU monitoring counters implemented in this component.
F 31 1 hnf_mpam_mbwumon_has_capture
DESC 0: MSMON_MBWU_CAPTURE is not implemented and there is no support for capture events in this component's MBWU monitor feature. 1: This component's MBWU monitor feature has an MSMON_MBWU_CAPTURE register for every MSMON_MBWU and supports the capture event behaviour.
R 0x10f0 64 - - por_hnf_ns_mpam_ecr
RESET 0x0 0x1
DESC MPAM Error Control Register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 1 hnf_ns_mpam_ecr_inten
DESC Interrupt Enable. When INTEN = 0, MPAM error interrupts are not generated. When INTEN = 1, MPAM error interrupts are generated.
R 0x10f8 64 - - por_hnf_ns_mpam_esr
RESET 0x0 0x8fffffff
DESC MPAM Error Status Register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_ns_mpam_esr_partid_mon
DESC PARTID captured if the error code captures PARTID. MON selector captured if the error code captures MON. Otherwise 0x0000.
F 16 8 hnf_ns_mpam_esr_pmg
DESC PMG captured if the error code captures PMG, otherwise 0x0000.
F 24 4 hnf_ns_mpam_esr_errcode
DESC Error code
F 31 1 hnf_ns_mpam_esr_ovrwr
DESC Overwritten. If 0 and ERRCODE is zero, no errors have occurred. If 0 and ERRCODE is non-zero, a single error has occurred and is recorded in this register. If 1 and ERRCODE is non-zero, multiple errors have occurred and this register records the most recent error. The state where this bit is 1 and ERRCODE is zero is not produced by hardware and is only reached when software writes this combination into this register.
R 0x1100 64 - - por_hnf_ns_mpamcfg_part_sel
RESET 0x0 0x1ffff
DESC MPAM partition configuration selection register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_part_sel_partid_sel
DESC Selects the partition ID to configure.
F 16 1 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_part_sel_internal
DESC If MPAMF_IDR.HAS_PARTID_NRW = 0, this field is RAZ/WI. If MPAMF_IDR.HAS_PARTID_NRW = 1, this bit decides how to interprete PARTID_SEL.
R 0x1108 64 - - por_hnf_ns_mpamcfg_cmax
RESET 0xfe00 0xfe00
DESC MPAM cache maximum capacity partition configuration register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 9 7 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_cmax_cmax
DESC Maximum cache capacity usage in fixed-point fraction of the cache capacity by the partition selected by MPAMCFG_PART_SEL.
R 0x1200 64 - - por_hnf_ns_mpamcfg_mbw_min
RESET 0x0 0xff00
DESC MPAM memory minimum bandwidth partitioning configuration register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 8 8 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_mbw_min_min
DESC Memory minimum bandwidth allocated to the partition selected by MPAMCFG_PART_SEL.
R 0x1208 64 - - por_hnf_ns_mpamcfg_mbw_max
RESET 0x0 0x8000ff00
DESC MPAM memory maximum bandwidth partitioning configuration register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 8 8 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_mbw_max_max
DESC Memory maximum bandwidth allocated to the partition selected by MPAMCFG_PART_SEL.
F 31 1 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_mbw_max_hardlim
DESC 0: When MAX bandwidth is exceeded, the partition may contend with a low preference for downstream bandwidth beyond its maximum bandwidth. 1: When MAX bandwidth is exceeded, the partition may not be use any more bandwidth until its memory bandwidth measurement falls below the maximum limit.
R 0x1220 64 - - por_hnf_ns_mpamcfg_mbw_winwd
RESET 0x0 0xffffff
DESC MPAM memory bandwidth partitioning window width register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 8 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_mbw_winwd_us_frac
DESC Memory bandwidth accounting period fractions of a microsecond.
F 8 16 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_mbw_winwd_us_int
DESC Memory bandwidth accounting period integer microseconds.
R 0x1400 64 - - por_hnf_ns_mpamcfg_pri
RESET 0x0 0xff00ff
DESC MPAM priority partitioning configuration register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 8 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_pri_intpri
DESC If HAS_INTPRI is 1, this field is a priority value applied internally inside this memory system component for transactions of the partition selected by MPAMCFG_PART_SEL.
F 16 8 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_pri_dspri
DESC If HAS_DSPRI is 1, this field is a priority value applied to downstream communications from this memory system component for transactions of the partition selected by MPAMCFG_PART_SEL.
R 0x1500 64 - - por_hnf_ns_mpamcfg_mbw_prop
RESET 0x0 0x800000ff
DESC Memory bandwidth proportional stride partitioning configuration register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 8 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_mbw_prop_stridem1
DESC Normalized cost of a bandwidth consumption by the partition. STRIDEM1 is the stride for the partition minus one.
F 31 1 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_mbw_prop_en
DESC 0: The selected partition is not regulated by proportional stride bandwidth partitioning. 1: The selected partition has bandwidth usage regulated by proportional stride bandwidth partitioning as controlled by STRIDEM1.
R 0x1600 64 - - por_hnf_ns_mpamcfg_intpartid
RESET 0x0 0x1ffff
DESC MPAM internal partition narrowing configuration register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_intpartid_intpartid
DESC This field contains the intPARTID mapped to the reqPARTID in MPAMCFG_PART_SEL.
F 16 1 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_intpartid_internal
DESC This bit must be 1 when written to the register. If written as 0, the write will not update the reqPARTID to intPARTID association.
R 0x1800 64 - - por_hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mon_sel
RESET 0x0 0xffff
DESC Memory system performance monitor selection register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mon_sel_mon_sel
DESC Selects the performance monitor to configure.
R 0x1808 64 - - por_hnf_ns_msmon_capt_evnt
RESET 0x0 0x3
DESC Memory system performance monitoring capture event generation register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 1 hnf_ns_msmon_capt_evnt_now
DESC When written as 1, this bit causes an event to all monitors in this memory system component with CAPT_EVNT set to the value of 7. When this bit is written as 0, no event is signalled.
F 1 1 hnf_ns_msmon_capt_evnt_all
DESC In secure version, if ALL written as 1 and NOW is also written as 1, signal a capture event to secure and non-secure monitors in this memory system component with CAPT_EVNT = 7. If written as 0 and NOW is written as 1, signal a capture event to secure monitors in this memory system component with CAPT_EVNT = 7. In non-secure version if NOW is written as 1, signal a capture event to non-secure monitors in this memory system component with CAPT_EVNT = 7.
R 0x1810 64 - - por_hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_csu_flt
RESET 0x0 0xffffff
DESC Memory system performance monitor configure cache storage usage monitor filter register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_csu_flt_partid
DESC Configures the cache storage usage performance monitor to a PARTID. The monitor selected by MSMON_CFG_MON_SEL.MON_SEL counts or measures the storage usage by cache lines labelled with both the configured PARTID and PMG.
F 16 8 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_csu_flt_pmg
DESC Configures the cache storage usage performance monitor to a PMG. The monitor selected by MSMON_CFG_MON_SEL.MON_SEL counts or measures storage usage by cache lines labelled with both the configured PARTID and PMG.
R 0x1818 64 - - por_hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl
RESET 0x43 0xfff300ff
DESC Memory system performance monitor configure cache storage usage monitor control register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 8 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_type
DESC Read-only: Constant type indicating the type of the monitor. CSU monitor is TYPE = 0x43.
F 16 1 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_match_partid
DESC 0: Monitor storage used by all PARTIDs. 1: Only monitor storage used with the PARTID matching MSMON_CFG_CSU_FLT.PARTID.
F 17 1 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_match_pmg
DESC 0: Monitor storage used by all PMG values. 1: Only monitor storage used with the PMG value matching MSMON_CFG_CSU_FLT.PMG.
F 20 4 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_subtype
DESC Not currently used for CSU monitors, but reserved for future use.
F 24 1 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_oflow_frz
DESC 0: Monitor count wraps on overflow. 1: Monitor count freezes on overflow. The frozen value may be 0 or another value if the monitor overflowed with an increment larger than 1.
F 25 1 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_oflow_intr
DESC 0: No interrupt. 1: On overflow, an implementation-specific interrupt is signalled.
F 26 1 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_oflow_status
DESC 0: No overflow has occurred. 1: At least one overflow has occurred since this bit was last written.
F 27 1 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_capt_reset
DESC Capture is not implemented for the CSU monitor type.
F 28 3 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_capt_evnt
DESC Select the event that triggers capture from the following: 0: No capture event is triggered. 1: External capture event 1 (optional but recommended)
F 31 1 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_en
DESC 0: The monitor is disabled and must not collect any information. 1: The monitor is enabled to collect information according to its configuration.
R 0x1820 64 - - por_hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mbwu_flt
RESET 0x0 0xffffff
DESC Memory system performance monitor configure memory bandwidth usage monitor filter register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mbwu_flt_partid
DESC Configures the memory bandwidth usage performance monitor to a PARTID. The monitor selected by MSMON_CFG_MON_SEL.MON_SEL counts or measures the memory bandwidth used by requests labelled with both the configured PARTID and PMG.
F 16 8 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mbwu_flt_pmg
DESC Configures the memory bandwidth usage performance monitor to a PMG. The monitor selected by MSMON_CFG_MON_SEL.MON_SEL counts or measures the memory bandwidth used by requests labelled with both the configured PARTID and PMG.
R 0x1828 64 - - por_hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl
RESET 0x42 0xfff300ff
DESC Memory system performance monitor configure memory bandwidth usage monitor control register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 8 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_type
DESC Read-only: Constant type indicating the type of the monitor. MBWU monitor is TYPE = 0x42.
F 16 1 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_match_partid
DESC 0: Monitor bandwidth used by all PARTIDs. 1: Only monitor bandwidth used with the PARTID matching MSMON_CFG_MBWU_FLT.PARTID.
F 17 1 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_match_pmg
DESC 0: Monitor bandwidth used by all PMG values. 1: Only monitor bandwidth used with the PMG value matching MSMON_CFG_CSU_FLT.PMG.
F 20 4 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_subtype
DESC A monitor can have other event matching criteria. The meaning of values in this field varies by monitor type. The MBWU monitor type supports: 0: Do not count any bandwidth. 1: Count bandwidth used by memory reads 2: Count bandwidth used by memory writes 3: Count bandwidth used by memory reads and memory writes All other values are reserved and behaviour of a monitor with SUBTYPE set to one of the reserved values is UNPREDICTABLE.
F 24 1 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_oflow_frz
DESC 0: Monitor count wraps on overflow. 1: Monitor count freezes on overflow. The frozen value may be 0 or another value if the monitor overflowed with an increment larger than 1.
F 25 1 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_oflow_intr
DESC 0: No interrupt. 1: On overflow, an implementation-specific interrupt is signalled.
F 26 1 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_oflow_status
DESC 0: No overflow has occurred. 1: At least one overflow has occurred since this bit was last written.
F 27 1 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_capt_reset
DESC 0: Monitor is not reset on capture. 1: Monitor is reset on capture.
F 28 3 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_capt_evnt
DESC Select the event that triggers capture from the following: 0: No capture event is triggered. 1: External capture event 1 (optional but recommended)
F 31 1 hnf_ns_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_en
DESC 0: The monitor is disabled and must not collect any information. 1: The monitor is enabled to collect information according to its configuration.
R 0x1840 64 - - por_hnf_ns_msmon_csu
RESET 0x0 0xffffffff
DESC Memory system performance monitor cache storage usage monitor register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 31 hnf_ns_msmon_csu_value
DESC Cache storage usage value if NRDY is 0. Invalid if NRDY is 1. VALUE is the cache storage usage in bytes.
F 31 1 hnf_ns_msmon_csu_nrdy
DESC Indicates that the monitor does not have accurate data, possibly because insufficient time has elapsed since the monitor was last configured.
R 0x1848 64 - - por_hnf_ns_msmon_csu_capture
RESET 0x0 0xffffffff
DESC Memory system performance monitor cache storage usage capture register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 31 hnf_ns_msmon_csu_vapture_value
DESC Cache storage usage value if NRDY is 0. Invalid if NRDY is 1. VALUE is the cache storage usage in bytes.
F 31 1 hnf_ns_msmon_csu_capture_nrdy
DESC Indicates that the monitor does not have accurate data, possibly because insufficient time has elapsed since the monitor was last configured.
R 0x1860 64 - - por_hnf_ns_msmon_mbwu
RESET 0x0 0xffffffff
DESC Memory system performance monitor memory bandwidth usage monitor register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 31 hnf_ns_msmon_mbwu_value
DESC Memory channel bandwidth value if NRDY is 0. Invalid if NRDY is 1. VALUE is the memory channel bandwidth usage in megabytes.
F 31 1 hnf_ns_msmon_mbwu_nrdy
DESC Indicates that the monitor does not have accurate data, possibly because insufficient time has elapsed since the monitor was last configured.
R 0x1868 64 - - por_hnf_ns_msmon_mbwu_capture
RESET 0x0 0xffffffff
DESC Memory system performance monitor memory bandwidth usage capture register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 31 hnf_ns_msmon_mbwu_capture_value
DESC Memory channel bandwidth value if NRDY is 0. Invalid if NRDY is 1. VALUE is the memory channel bandwidth usage in megabytes.
F 31 1 hnf_ns_msmon_mbwu_capture_nrdy
DESC Indicates that the monitor does not have accurate data, possibly because insufficient time has elapsed since the monitor was last configured.
R 0x2000 64 - - por_hnf_ns_mpamcfg_cpbm
RESET 0xffff 0xffff
DESC MPAM cache portion bitmap partition configuration register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_ns_mpamcfg_cpbm_cpbm
DESC Bitmap of portions of cache capacity allocable by the partition selected by MPAMCFG_PART_SEL. NOTE: CPBM can not be all zeros for any PARTID.
ENDGROUP
GROUP por_hnf_mpam_s_registers
BASE 0x0
RANGE 0x10000
R 0x0 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_s_node_info
RESET 0x8 0xffffffffffff
DESC Provides component identification information.
F 0 16 node_type
DESC CMN-600 node type identifier
F 16 16 node_id
DESC Component node ID
PAR NODEID_PARAM
F 32 16 logical_id
DESC Component logical ID
PAR LOGICALID_PARAM
R 0x80 64 RO - por_hnf_mpam_s_child_info
RESET 0x0 0xffffffff
DESC Provides component child identification information.
F 0 16 child_count
DESC Number of child nodes; used in discovery process
F 16 16 child_ptr_offset
DESC Starting register offset which contains pointers to the child nodes
R 0x980 64 - S por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override
RESET 0x0 0x40
DESC Allows non-secure access to predefined groups of secure registers.
F 6 1 mpam
DESC Allows non-secure access to secure MPAM registers
R 0x1000 64 RO - por_hnf_s_mpam_idr
RESET 0x1000f 0xefffffff
DESC MPAM features ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_mpam_partid_max
DESC Maximum value of non-secure PARTID supported by this HN-F
PAR HNF_MPAM_NS_PARTID_PARAM
F 16 8 hnf_mpam_pmg_max
DESC Maximum value of non-secure PMG supported by this HN-F
PAR HNF_MPAM_NS_PMG_PARAM
F 24 1 hnf_mpam_has_ccap_part
DESC 0: MPAM cache maximum capacity partitioning is not supported 1: MPAM cache maximum capacity partitioning is supported
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_CCAP_PART_PARAM
F 25 1 hnf_mpam_has_cpor_part
DESC 0: MPAM cache portion partitioning is not supported 1: MPAM cache portion partitioning is supported
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_CPOR_PART_PARAM
F 26 1 hnf_mpam_has_mbw_part
DESC 0: MPAM memory bandwidth partitioning is not supported 1: MPAM memory bandwidth partitioning is supported
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_MBW_PART_PARAM
F 27 1 hnf_mpam_has_pri_part
DESC 0: MPAM priority partitioning is not supported 1: MPAM priority partitioning is supported
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_PRI_PART_PARAM
F 29 1 hnf_mpam_has_impl_idr
DESC 0: MPAM implementation specific partitioning features not supported 1: MPAM implementation specific partitioning features supported
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_IMPL_IDR_PARAM
F 30 1 hnf_mpam_has_msmon
DESC 0: MPAM performance monitoring is not supported 1: MPAM performance monitoring is supported
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_MSMON_PARAM
F 31 1 hnf_mpam_has_partid_nrw
DESC 0: HN-F does not support MPAM PARTID Narrowing 1: HN-F supports MPAM PARTID Narrowing
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_PARTID_NRW_PARAM
R 0x1008 64 RO S por_hnf_mpam_sidr
RESET 0x1000f 0xffffff
DESC MPAM features Secure ID register.  This is Secure (S) register only.
F 0 16 hnf_mpam_s_partid_max
DESC Maximum value of secure PARTID supported by this HN-F
PAR HNF_MPAM_S_PARTID_PARAM
F 16 8 hnf_mpam_s_pmg_max
DESC Maximum value of secure PMG supported by this HN-F
PAR HNF_MPAM_S_PMG_PARAM
R 0x1018 64 RO - por_hnf_s_mpam_iidr
RESET 0x43b 0xffffffff
DESC MPAM Implementation ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 12 hnf_mpam_iidr_implementer
DESC Implementation defined value identifying company that implemented MPAM memory system component
F 12 4 hnf_mpam_iidr_revision
DESC Implementation defined value identifying minor revision of the product
F 16 4 hnf_mpam_iidr_variant
DESC Implementation defined value identifying major revision of the product
F 20 12 hnf_mpam_iidr_productid
DESC Implementation defined value identifying MPAM memory system component
R 0x1020 64 RO - por_hnf_s_mpam_aidr
RESET 0x10 0xff
DESC MPAM architecture ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 4 hnf_mpam_aidr_arch_minor_rev
DESC Minor revision of the MPAM architecture that this memory system component implements
F 4 4 hnf_mpam_aidr_arch_major_rev
DESC Major revision of the MPAM architecture that this memory system component implements
R 0x1028 64 RO - por_hnf_s_mpam_impl_idr
RESET 0x0 0xffffffff
DESC MPAM Implementation defined partitioning feature ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 32 hnf_mpam_impl_idr
DESC Implementation defined partitioning features.
R 0x1030 64 RO - por_hnf_s_mpam_cpor_idr
RESET 0x10 0xffff
DESC MPAM cache portion partitioning ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_mpam_cpor_idr_cpbm_wd
DESC Number of bits in the cache portion partitioning bit map of this device.
PAR HNF_MPAM_CPBM_WD_PARAM
R 0x1038 64 RO - por_hnf_s_mpam_ccap_idr
RESET 0x7 0x3f
DESC MPAM cache capacity partitioning ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 6 hnf_mpam_ccap_idr_cmax_wd
DESC Number of fractional bits implemented in the cache capacity partitioning.
PAR HNF_MPAM_CMAX_WD_PARAM
R 0x1040 64 RO - por_hnf_s_mpam_mbw_idr
RESET 0x0 0x1fff7c3f
DESC MPAM Memory Bandwidth partitioning ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 6 hnf_mpam_mbw_idr_bwa_wd
DESC Number of implemented bits in bandwidth allocation fields: MIN, MAX, and STRIDE. Value must be between 1 to 16
F 10 1 hnf_mpam_mbw_idr_has_min
DESC 0: There is no minimum memory bandwidth control and no MPAMCFG_MBW_MIN register 1: MPAMCFG_MBW_MIN register exists and minimum memory bandwidth allocation scheme is supported.
F 11 1 hnf_mpam_mbw_idr_has_max
DESC 0: There is no maximum memory bandwidth control and no MPAMCFG_MBW_MAX register 1: MPAMCFG_MBW_MAX register exists and maximum memory bandwidth allocation scheme is supported.
F 12 1 hnf_mpam_mbw_idr_has_pbm
DESC 0: There is no memory bandwidth portion control and no MPAMCFG_MBW_PBM register 1: MPAMCFG_MBW_PBM register exists and memory bandwidth portion allocation scheme is supported.
F 13 1 hnf_mpam_mbw_idr_has_prop
DESC 0: There is no memory bandwidth proportional stride control and no MPAMCFG_MBW_PROP register 1: MPAMCFG_MBW_PROP register exists and memory bandwidth proportional stride memory bandwidth allocation scheme is supported.
F 14 1 hnf_mpam_mbw_idr_windwr
DESC 0: The bandwidth accounting period should be read from MPAMCFG_MBW_WINDWR register, which might be fixed. 1: The bandwidth accounting width is readable and writable per partition in MPAMCFG_MBW_WINDWR register.
F 16 13 hnf_mpam_mbw_idr_bwpbm_wd
DESC Number of bits indication portions in MPAMCFG_MBW_PBM register.
R 0x1048 64 RO - por_hnf_s_mpam_pri_idr
RESET 0x0 0x3f303f3
DESC MPAM Priority partitioning ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 1 hnf_mpam_pri_idr_has_intpri
DESC 0: This memory system component supports priority, but doesn't have an internal priority field in MPAMCFG_PRI. 1: This memory system component supports internal priority and has an INTPRI field.
F 1 1 hnf_mpam_pri_idr_intpri_0_is_low
DESC 0: In the INTPRI field, a value of 0 means highest priority. 1: In the INTPRI field, a value of 0 means lowest priority.
F 4 6 hnf_mpam_pri_idr_intpri_wd
DESC Number of bits in the internal priority field (INTPRI) in MPAMCFG_PRI.
F 16 1 hnf_mpam_pri_idr_has_dspri
DESC 0: This memory system component supports priority, but doesn't have a downstream priority (DSPRI) field in MPAMCFG_PRI. 1: This memory system component supports downstream priority and has an DSPRI field.
F 17 1 hnf_mpam_pri_idr_has_dspri_0_is_low
DESC 0: In the DSPRI field, a value of 0 means highest priority. 1: In the DSPRI field, a value of 0 means lowest priority.
F 20 6 hnf_mpam_pri_idr_dspri_wd
DESC Number of bits in downstream priority field (DSPRI) in MPAMCFG_PRI.
R 0x1050 64 RO - por_hnf_s_mpam_partid_nrw_idr
RESET 0x0 0xffff
DESC MPAM PARTID narrowing ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_mpam_partid_nrw_idr_intpartid_max
DESC This field indicates the largest intPARTID supported in this component.
R 0x1080 64 RO - por_hnf_s_mpam_msmon_idr
RESET 0x80000000 0x80030000
DESC MPAM performance monitoring ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 16 1 hnf_mpam_msmon_csu
DESC This component has a performance monitor for Cache Storage Usage by PARTID and PMG.
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_MSMON_CSU_PARAM
F 17 1 hnf_mpam_msmon_mbwu
DESC This component has a performance monitor for Memory Bandwidth Usage by PARTID and PMG.
PAR HNF_MPAM_HAS_MSMON_MBWU_PARAM
F 31 1 hnf_mpam_msmon_has_local_capt_evnt
DESC Has the local capture event generator and the MSMON_CAPT_EVNT register.
R 0x1088 64 RO - por_hnf_s_mpam_csumon_idr
RESET 0x80000004 0x8000ffff
DESC MPAM cache storage usage monitor ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_mpam_csumon_num_mon
DESC The number of CSU monitoring counters implemented in this component.
PAR HNF_MPAM_NUM_CSUMON_PARAM
F 31 1 hnf_mpam_csumon_has_capture
DESC 0: MSMON_CSU_CAPTURE is not implemented and there is no support for capture events in this component's CSU monitor feature. 1: This component's CSU monitor feature has an MSMON_CSU_CAPTURE register for every MSMON_CSU and supports the capture event behaviour.
R 0x1090 64 RO - por_hnf_s_mpam_mbwumon_idr
RESET 0x0 0x8000ffff
DESC MPAM memory bandwidth usage monitor ID register. This is a shared register for S and NS
F 0 16 hnf_mpam_mbwumon_num_mon
DESC The number of MBWU monitoring counters implemented in this component.
F 31 1 hnf_mpam_mbwumon_has_capture
DESC 0: MSMON_MBWU_CAPTURE is not implemented and there is no support for capture events in this component's MBWU monitor feature. 1: This component's MBWU monitor feature has an MSMON_MBWU_CAPTURE register for every MSMON_MBWU and supports the capture event behaviour.
R 0x10f0 64 - S por_hnf_s_mpam_ecr
RESET 0x0 0x1
DESC MPAM Error Control Register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 0 1 hnf_s_mpam_ecr_inten
DESC Interrupt Enable. When INTEN = 0, MPAM error interrupts are not generated. When INTEN = 1, MPAM error interrupts are generated.
R 0x10f8 64 - S por_hnf_s_mpam_esr
RESET 0x0 0x8fffffff
DESC MPAM Error Status Register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 0 16 hnf_s_mpam_esr_partid_mon
DESC PARTID captured if the error code captures PARTID. MON selector captured if the error code captures MON. Otherwise 0x0000.
F 16 8 hnf_s_mpam_esr_pmg
DESC PMG captured if the error code captures PMG, otherwise 0x0000.
F 24 4 hnf_s_mpam_esr_errcode
DESC Error code
F 31 1 hnf_s_mpam_esr_ovrwr
DESC Overwritten. If 0 and ERRCODE is zero, no errors have occurred. If 0 and ERRCODE is non-zero, a single error has occurred and is recorded in this register. If 1 and ERRCODE is non-zero, multiple errors have occurred and this register records the most recent error. The state where this bit is 1 and ERRCODE is zero is not produced by hardware and is only reached when software writes this combination into this register.
R 0x1100 64 - S por_hnf_s_mpamcfg_part_sel
RESET 0x0 0x1ffff
DESC MPAM partition configuration selection register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 0 16 hnf_s_mpamcfg_part_sel_partid_sel
DESC Selects the partition ID to configure.
F 16 1 hnf_s_mpamcfg_part_sel_internal
DESC If MPAMF_IDR.HAS_PARTID_NRW = 0, this field is RAZ/WI. If MPAMF_IDR.HAS_PARTID_NRW = 1, this bit decides how to interprete PARTID_SEL.
R 0x1108 64 - S por_hnf_s_mpamcfg_cmax
RESET 0xfe00 0xfe00
DESC MPAM cache maximum capacity partition configuration register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 9 7 hnf_s_mpamcfg_cmax_cmax
DESC Maximum cache capacity usage in fixed-point fraction of the cache capacity by the partition selected by MPAMCFG_PART_SEL.
R 0x1200 64 - S por_hnf_s_mpamcfg_mbw_min
RESET 0x0 0xff00
DESC MPAM memory minimum bandwidth partitioning configuration register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 8 8 hnf_s_mpamcfg_mbw_min_min
DESC Memory minimum bandwidth allocated to the partition selected by MPAMCFG_PART_SEL.
R 0x1208 64 - S por_hnf_s_mpamcfg_mbw_max
RESET 0x0 0x8000ff00
DESC MPAM memory maximum bandwidth partitioning configuration register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 8 8 hnf_s_mpamcfg_mbw_max_max
DESC Memory maximum bandwidth allocated to the partition selected by MPAMCFG_PART_SEL.
F 31 1 hnf_s_mpamcfg_mbw_max_hardlim
DESC 0: When MAX bandwidth is exceeded, the partition may contend with a low preference for downstream bandwidth beyond its maximum bandwidth. 1: When MAX bandwidth is exceeded, the partition may not be use any more bandwidth until its memory bandwidth measurement falls below the maximum limit.
R 0x1220 64 - S por_hnf_s_mpamcfg_mbw_winwd
RESET 0x0 0xffffff
DESC MPAM memory bandwidth partitioning window width register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 0 8 hnf_s_mpamcfg_mbw_winwd_us_frac
DESC Memory bandwidth accounting period fractions of a microsecond.
F 8 16 hnf_s_mpamcfg_mbw_winwd_us_int
DESC Memory bandwidth accounting period integer microseconds.
R 0x1400 64 - S por_hnf_s_mpamcfg_pri
RESET 0x0 0xff00ff
DESC MPAM priority partitioning configuration register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 0 8 hnf_s_mpamcfg_pri_intpri
DESC If HAS_INTPRI is 1, this field is a priority value applied internally inside this memory system component for transactions of the partition selected by MPAMCFG_PART_SEL.
F 16 8 hnf_s_mpamcfg_pri_dspri
DESC If HAS_DSPRI is 1, this field is a priority value applied to downstream communications from this memory system component for transactions of the partition selected by MPAMCFG_PART_SEL.
R 0x1500 64 - S por_hnf_s_mpamcfg_mbw_prop
RESET 0x0 0x800000ff
DESC Memory bandwidth proportional stride partitioning configuration register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 0 8 hnf_s_mpamcfg_mbw_prop_stridem1
DESC Normalized cost of a bandwidth consumption by the partition. STRIDEM1 is the stride for the partition minus one.
F 31 1 hnf_s_mpamcfg_mbw_prop_en
DESC 0: The selected partition is not regulated by proportional stride bandwidth partitioning. 1: The selected partition has bandwidth usage regulated by proportional stride bandwidth partitioning as controlled by STRIDEM1.
R 0x1600 64 - S por_hnf_s_mpamcfg_intpartid
RESET 0x0 0x1ffff
DESC MPAM internal partition narrowing configuration register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 0 16 hnf_s_mpamcfg_intpartid_intpartid
DESC This field contains the intPARTID mapped to the reqPARTID in MPAMCFG_PART_SEL.
F 16 1 hnf_s_mpamcfg_intpartid_internal
DESC This bit must be 1 when written to the register. If written as 0, the write will not update the reqPARTID to intPARTID association.
R 0x1800 64 - S por_hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mon_sel
RESET 0x0 0xffff
DESC Memory system performance monitor selection register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 0 16 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mon_sel_mon_sel
DESC Selects the performance monitor to configure.
R 0x1808 64 - S por_hnf_s_msmon_capt_evnt
RESET 0x0 0x3
DESC Memory system performance monitoring capture event generation register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 0 1 hnf_s_msmon_capt_evnt_now
DESC When written as 1, this bit causes an event to all monitors in this memory system component with CAPT_EVNT set to the value of 7. When this bit is written as 0, no event is signalled.
F 1 1 hnf_s_msmon_capt_evnt_all
DESC In secure version, if ALL written as 1 and NOW is also written as 1, signal a capture event to secure and non-secure monitors in this memory system component with CAPT_EVNT = 7. If written as 0 and NOW is written as 1, signal a capture event to secure monitors in this memory system component with CAPT_EVNT = 7. In non-secure version if NOW is written as 1, signal a capture event to non-secure monitors in this memory system component with CAPT_EVNT = 7.
R 0x1810 64 - S por_hnf_s_msmon_cfg_csu_flt
RESET 0x0 0xffffff
DESC Memory system performance monitor configure cache storage usage monitor filter register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 0 16 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_csu_flt_partid
DESC Configures the cache storage usage performance monitor to a PARTID. The monitor selected by MSMON_CFG_MON_SEL.MON_SEL counts or measures the storage usage by cache lines labelled with both the configured PARTID and PMG.
F 16 8 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_csu_flt_pmg
DESC Configures the cache storage usage performance monitor to a PMG. The monitor selected by MSMON_CFG_MON_SEL.MON_SEL counts or measures storage usage by cache lines labelled with both the configured PARTID and PMG.
R 0x1818 64 - S por_hnf_s_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl
RESET 0x43 0xfff300ff
DESC Memory system performance monitor configure cache storage usage monitor control register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 0 8 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_type
DESC Read-only: Constant type indicating the type of the monitor. CSU monitor is TYPE = 0x43.
F 16 1 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_match_partid
DESC 0: Monitor storage used by all PARTIDs. 1: Only monitor storage used with the PARTID matching MSMON_CFG_CSU_FLT.PARTID.
F 17 1 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_match_pmg
DESC 0: Monitor storage used by all PMG values. 1: Only monitor storage used with the PMG value matching MSMON_CFG_CSU_FLT.PMG.
F 20 4 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_subtype
DESC Not currently used for CSU monitors, but reserved for future use.
F 24 1 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_oflow_frz
DESC 0: Monitor count wraps on overflow. 1: Monitor count freezes on overflow. The frozen value may be 0 or another value if the monitor overflowed with an increment larger than 1.
F 25 1 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_oflow_intr
DESC 0: No interrupt. 1: On overflow, an implementation-specific interrupt is signalled.
F 26 1 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_oflow_status
DESC 0: No overflow has occurred. 1: At least one overflow has occurred since this bit was last written.
F 27 1 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_capt_reset
DESC Capture is not implemented for the CSU monitor type.
F 28 3 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_capt_evnt
DESC Select the event that triggers capture from the following: 0: No capture event is triggered. 1: External capture event 1 (optional but recommended)
F 31 1 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_csu_ctl_en
DESC 0: The monitor is disabled and must not collect any information. 1: The monitor is enabled to collect information according to its configuration.
R 0x1820 64 - S por_hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mbwu_flt
RESET 0x0 0xffffff
DESC Memory system performance monitor configure memory bandwidth usage monitor filter register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 0 16 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mbwu_flt_partid
DESC Configures the memory bandwidth usage performance monitor to a PARTID. The monitor selected by MSMON_CFG_MON_SEL.MON_SEL counts or measures the memory bandwidth used by requests labelled with both the configured PARTID and PMG.
F 16 8 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mbwu_flt_pmg
DESC Configures the memory bandwidth usage performance monitor to a PMG. The monitor selected by MSMON_CFG_MON_SEL.MON_SEL counts or measures the memory bandwidth used by requests labelled with both the configured PARTID and PMG.
R 0x1828 64 - S por_hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl
RESET 0x42 0xfff300ff
DESC Memory system performance monitor configure memory bandwidth usage monitor control register. This register is a banked seperately for S and NS
SGO por_hnf_mpam_s_secure_register_groups_override.mpam
F 0 8 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_type
DESC Read-only: Constant type indicating the type of the monitor. MBWU monitor is TYPE = 0x42.
F 16 1 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_match_partid
DESC 0: Monitor bandwidth used by all PARTIDs. 1: Only monitor bandwidth used with the PARTID matching MSMON_CFG_MBWU_FLT.PARTID.
F 17 1 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_match_pmg
DESC 0: Monitor bandwidth used by all PMG values. 1: Only monitor bandwidth used with the PMG value matching MSMON_CFG_CSU_FLT.PMG.
F 20 4 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_subtype
DESC A monitor can have other event matching criteria. The meaning of values in this field varies by monitor type. The MBWU monitor type supports: 0: Do not count any bandwidth. 1: Count bandwidth used by memory reads 2: Count bandwidth used by memory writes 3: Count bandwidth used by memory reads and memory writes All other values are reserved and behaviour of a monitor with SUBTYPE set to one of the reserved values is UNPREDICTABLE.
F 24 1 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_oflow_frz
DESC 0: Monitor count wraps on overflow. 1: Monitor count freezes on overflow. The frozen value may be 0 or another value if the monitor overflowed with an increment larger than 1.
F 25 1 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_oflow_intr
DESC 0: No interrupt. 1: On overflow, an implementation-specific interrupt is signalled.
F 26 1 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_oflow_status
DESC 0: No overflow has occurred. 1: At least one overflow has occurred since this bit was last written.
F 27 1 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_capt_reset
DESC 0: Monitor is not reset on capture. 1: Monitor is reset on capture.
F 28 3 hnf_s_msmon_cfg_mbwu_ctl_capt_evnt
