R 0x3000 64 RO S por_mxp_errfr
RESET 0xa5 0x7cff
DESC Functions as the error feature register.
SGO por_mxp_secure_register_groups_override.ras_secure_access_override
F 0 2 ED
DESC Error detection
F 2 2 DE
DESC Deferred errors for data poison
F 4 2 UI
DESC Uncorrected error interrupt
F 6 2 FI
DESC Fault handling interrupt
F 10 2 CFI
DESC Corrected error interrupt
F 12 3 CEC
DESC Standard corrected error count mechanism 3'b000: Does not implement standardized error counter model
R 0x3008 64 - S por_mxp_errctlr
RESET 0x0 0x10f
DESC Functions as the error control register. Controls whether specific error-handling interrupts and error detection/deferment are enabled.
SGO por_mxp_secure_register_groups_override.ras_secure_access_override
F 0 1 ED
DESC Enables error detection as specified in por_mxp_errfr.ED
F 1 1 DE
DESC Enables error deferment as specified in por_mxp_errfr.DE
F 2 1 UI
DESC Enables uncorrected error interrupt as specified in por_mxp_errfr.UI
F 3 1 FI
DESC Enables fault handling interrupt for all detected deferred errors as specified in por_mxp_errfr.FI
F 8 1 CFI
DESC Enables corrected error interrupt as specified in por_mxp_errfr.CFI
R 0x3010 64 - S por_mxp_errstatus
RESET 0x0 0xed800000
DESC Functions as the error status register. AV and MV bits must be cleared in the same cycle, otherwise the error record does not have a consistent view.
SGO por_mxp_secure_register_groups_override.ras_secure_access_override
F 31 1 AV W1C
DESC Address register valid; writes to this bit are ignored if any of the UE, DE, or CE bits are set to 1, and the highest priority are not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: Address is valid 1'b0: Address is not valid
F 30 1 V W1C
DESC Register valid; writes to this bit are ignored if any of the UE, DE, or CE bits are set to 1, and are not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: At least one error recorded; register is valid 1'b0: No errors recorded
F 29 1 UE W1C
DESC Uncorrected errors; writes to this bit are ignored if the OF bit is set to 1, and is not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: At least one error detected that is not corrected and is not deferred to a slave 1'b0: No uncorrected errors detected
F 27 1 OF W1C
DESC Overflow; asserted when multiple errors of the highest priority type are detected; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: More than one error detected 1'b0: Only one error of the highest priority type detected as described by UE/DE/CE fields
F 26 1 MV W1C
DESC por_mxp_errmisc valid; writes to this bit are ignored if any of the UE, DE, or CE bits are set to 1, and the highest priority are not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: Miscellaneous registers are valid 1'b0: Miscellaneous registers are not valid
F 24 1 CE W1C
DESC Corrected errors; writes to this bit are ignored if the OF bit is set to 1, and is not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: At least one transient corrected error recorded 1'b0: No corrected errors recorded
F 23 1 DE W1C
DESC Deferred errors; writes to this bit are ignored if the OF bit is set to 1, and is not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: At least one error is not corrected and is deferred 1'b0: No errors deferred
R 0x3028 64 - S por_mxp_errmisc
RESET 0x0 0x87ff0000007fffff
DESC Functions as the miscellaneous error register. Contains miscellaneous information about deferred/uncorrected errors.
SGO por_mxp_secure_register_groups_override.ras_secure_access_override
F 63 1 TLPMSG
DESC Error flit TLPMSG Status
F 48 11 TGTID
DESC Error flit target ID
F 16 7 OPCODE
DESC Error flit opcode
F 5 11 SRCID
DESC Error flit source ID
F 0 5 ERRSRC
DESC Error source for Mesh With Replicated Channels: Bits [4:2]: Transaction type 3'b000: REQ 3'b001: RSP 3'b010: SNP 3'b011: DAT 3'b100: REQ2 3'b101: RSP2 3'b110: SNP2 3'b111: DAT2 Bits [1:0]: Port 2'b00:  Port 0 2'b01:  Port 1 2'b10:  Port 2 2'b11:  Port 3
Mesh Without Replicated Channels: Bits [4:2]: Transaction type 3'b000: REQ 3'b001: RSP 3'b010: SNP 3'b011: DAT 3'b100: Reserved 3'b101: Reserved 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved Bits [1:0]: Port 2'b00:  Port 0 2'b01:  Port 1 2'b10:  Port 2 2'b11:  Port 3
Mesh With Single MXP (1x1 Mesh): Bits [4:3]: Transaction type 2'b00:  REQ 2'b01:  RSP 2'b10:  SNP 2'b11:  DAT Bits [2:0]: Port 3'b000: Port 0 3'b001: Port 1 3'b010: Port 2 3'b011: Port 3 3'b100: Port 4 3'b101: Port 5
R 0x3030 64 WO S por_mxp_p0_byte_par_err_inj
RESET 0x0 0x1f
DESC Functions as the byte parity error injection register for XP port 0.
F 0 5 p0_byte_parity_err_inj
DESC Specifies a byte lane; once this register is written, a byte parity error is injected in the specified byte lane on the next DAT flit upload NOTE: Only applicable if an RN-F is attached to port 0. Byte parity error is only injected if the RN-F is configured to not support Datacheck.
R 0x3038 64 WO S por_mxp_p1_byte_par_err_inj
RESET 0x0 0x1f
DESC Functions as the byte parity error injection register for XP port 1.
F 0 5 p1_byte_parity_err_inj
DESC Specifies a byte lane; once this register is written, a byte parity error is injected in the specified byte lane on the next DAT flit upload NOTE: Only applicable if an RN-F is attached to port 1. Byte parity error is only injected if the RN-F is configured to not support Datacheck.
R 0x3040 64 WO S por_mxp_p2_byte_par_err_inj
RESET 0x0 0x1f
DESC Functions as the byte parity error injection register for XP port 2.
F 0 5 p2_byte_parity_err_inj
DESC Specifies a byte lane; once this register is written, a byte parity error is injected in the specified byte lane on the next DAT flit upload NOTE: Only applicable if an RN-F is attached to port 2. Byte parity error is only injected if the RN-F is configured to not support Datacheck.
R 0x3048 64 WO S por_mxp_p3_byte_par_err_inj
RESET 0x0 0x1f
DESC Functions as the byte parity error injection register for XP port 3.
F 0 5 p3_byte_parity_err_inj
DESC Specifies a byte lane; once this register is written, a byte parity error is injected in the specified byte lane on the next DAT flit upload NOTE: Only applicable if an RN-F is attached to port 3. Byte parity error is only injected if the RN-F is configured to not support Datacheck.
R 0x3050 64 WO S por_mxp_p4_byte_par_err_inj
RESET 0x0 0x1f
DESC Functions as the byte parity error injection register for XP port 4.
F 0 5 p4_byte_parity_err_inj
DESC Specifies a byte lane; once this register is written, a byte parity error is injected in the specified byte lane on the next DAT flit upload NOTE: Only applicable if an RN-F is attached to port 4. Byte parity error is only injected if the RN-F is configured to not support Datacheck.
R 0x3058 64 WO S por_mxp_p5_byte_par_err_inj
RESET 0x0 0x1f
DESC Functions as the byte parity error injection register for XP port 5.
F 0 5 p5_byte_parity_err_inj
DESC Specifies a byte lane; once this register is written, a byte parity error is injected in the specified byte lane on the next DAT flit upload NOTE: Only applicable if an RN-F is attached to port 5. Byte parity error is only injected if the RN-F is configured to not support Datacheck.
R 0x3100 64 RO - por_mxp_errfr_NS
RESET 0xa5 0x7cff
DESC Functions as the non-secure error feature register.
F 0 2 ED
DESC Error detection
F 2 2 DE
DESC Deferred errors for data poison
F 4 2 UI
DESC Uncorrected error interrupt
F 6 2 FI
DESC Fault handling interrupt
F 10 2 CFI
DESC Corrected error interrupt
F 12 3 CEC
DESC Standard corrected error count mechanism 3'b000: Does not implement standardized error counter model
R 0x3108 64 - - por_mxp_errctlr_NS
RESET 0x0 0x10f
DESC Functions as the non-secure error control register. Controls whether specific error-handling interrupts and error detection/deferment are enabled.
F 0 1 ED
DESC Enables error detection as specified in por_mxp_errfr_NS.ED
F 1 1 DE
DESC Enables error deferment as specified in por_mxp_errfr_NS.DE
F 2 1 UI
DESC Enables uncorrected error interrupt as specified in por_mxp_errfr_NS.UI
F 3 1 FI
DESC Enables fault handling interrupt for all detected deferred errors as specified in por_mxp_errfr_NS.FI
F 8 1 CFI
DESC Enables corrected error interrupt as specified in por_mxp_errfr_NS.CFI
R 0x3110 64 - - por_mxp_errstatus_NS
RESET 0x0 0xed800000
DESC Functions as the non-secure error status register.
F 31 1 AV W1C
DESC Address register valid; writes to this bit are ignored if any of the UE, DE, or CE bits are set to 1, and the highest priority are not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: Address is valid 1'b0: Address is not valid
F 30 1 V W1C
DESC Register valid; writes to this bit are ignored if any of the UE, DE, or CE bits are set to 1, and are not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: At least one error recorded; register is valid 1'b0: No errors recorded
F 29 1 UE W1C
DESC Uncorrected errors; writes to this bit are ignored if the OF bit is set to 1, and is not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: At least one error detected that is not corrected and is not deferred to a slave 1'b0: No uncorrected errors detected
F 27 1 OF W1C
DESC Overflow; asserted when multiple errors of the highest priority type are detected; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: More than one error detected 1'b0: Only one error of the highest priority type detected as described by UE/DE/CE fields
F 26 1 MV W1C
DESC por_mxp_errmisc_NS valid; writes to this bit are ignored if any of the UE, DE, or CE bits are set to 1, and the highest priority are not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: Miscellaneous registers are valid 1'b0: Miscellaneous registers are not valid
F 24 1 CE W1C
DESC Corrected errors; writes to this bit are ignored if the OF bit is set to 1, and is not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: At least one transient corrected error recorded 1'b0: No corrected errors recorded
F 23 1 DE W1C
DESC Deferred errors; writes to this bit are ignored if the OF bit is set to 1, and is not cleared to 0 in the same write; write a 1 to clear 1'b1: At least one error is not corrected and is deferred 1'b0: No errors deferred
R 0x3128 64 - - por_mxp_errmisc_NS
RESET 0x0 0x87ff0000007fffff
DESC Functions as the non-secure miscellaneous error register. Contains miscellaneous information about deferred/uncorrected errors.
F 63 1 TLPMSG
DESC Error flit TLPMSG Status
F 48 11 TGTID
DESC Error flit target ID
F 16 7 OPCODE
DESC Error flit opcode
F 5 11 SRCID
DESC Error flit source ID
F 0 5 ERRSRC
DESC Error source for Mesh With Replicated Channels: Bits [4:2]: Transaction type 3'b000: REQ 3'b001: RSP 3'b010: SNP 3'b011: DAT 3'b100: REQ2 3'b101: RSP2 3'b110: SNP2 3'b111: DAT2 Bits [1:0]: Port 2'b00:  Port 0 2'b01:  Port 1 2'b10:  Port 2 2'b11:  Port 3
Mesh Without Replicated Channels: Bits [4:2]: Transaction type 3'b000: REQ 3'b001: RSP 3'b010: SNP 3'b011: DAT 3'b100: Reserved 3'b101: Reserved 3'b110: Reserved 3'b111: Reserved Bits [1:0]: Port 2'b00:  Port 0 2'b01:  Port 1 2'b10:  Port 2 2'b11:  Port 3
Mesh With Single MXP (1x1 Mesh): Bits [4:3]: Transaction type 2'b00:  REQ 2'b01:  RSP 2'b10:  SNP 2'b11:  DAT Bits [2:0]: Port 3'b000: Port 0 3'b001: Port 1 3'b010: Port 2 3'b011: Port 3 3'b100: Port 4 3'b101: Port 5
ENDGROUP
GROUP por_rnd_registers
BASE 0x0
RANGE 0x10000
R 0x0 64 RO - por_rnd_node_info
RESET 0xd 0xffffffffffff
DESC Provides component identification information.
F 0 16 node_type
DESC CMN-600 node type identifier
F 16 16 node_id
DESC Component node ID
PAR NODEID_PARAM
F 32 16 logical_id
DESC Component logical ID
PAR LOGICALID_PARAM
R 0x80 64 RO - por_rnd_child_info
RESET 0x0 0xffffffff
DESC Provides component child identification information.
F 0 16 child_count
DESC Number of child nodes; used in discovery process
F 16 16 child_ptr_offset
DESC Starting register offset which contains pointers to the child nodes
R 0x900 64 RO - por_rnd_unit_info
RESET 0x80012001808020 0xffffffffffffffff
DESC Provides component identification information for RN-D.
F 0 10 num_wr_reqs
DESC Number of outstanding write requests
PAR RNID_NUM_WR_REQ_PARAM
F 10 10 num_rd_reqs
DESC Number of outstanding read requests
PAR RNID_NUM_RD_REQ_PARAM
F 20 10 num_rd_bufs
DESC Number of read data buffers
PAR RNID_NUM_RD_BUF_PARAM
F 30 10 ax_data_width
DESC AXI interface data width in bits
PAR RNID_AXDATA_WIDTH_PARAM
F 40 1 ax_datapoison_en
DESC Data Poison enable on ACE-Lite/AXI4 interface 1'b1: Enabled 1'b0: Not enabled
PAR RNID_AXDATAPOISON_EN_PARAM
F 41 1 force_rdb_prealloc
DESC Force read data buffer preallocation 1'b1: yes 1'b0: no
PAR RNID_FORCE_RDB_PREALLOC_PARAM
F 42 2 a4s_num
DESC Number of AXI4Stream interfaces present
PAR RNI_A4S_NUM_PARAM
F 44 10 a4s_logicalid_base
DESC AXI4Stream interfaces logical ID base
PAR RNI_A4S_LOGICALID_BASE_PARAM
F 54 10 num_atomic_bufs
DESC Number of atomic data buffers
PAR RNID_NUM_ATOMIC_BUF_PARAM
R 0x908 64 RO - por_rnd_unit_info2
RESET 0x20b 0x7fffff
DESC Provides additonal component identification information for RN-D.
F 0 6 id_width
DESC AXI ID width for ACE-Lite slave ports
PAR RNID_ID_WIDTH_PARAM
F 6 6 num_prealloc_bufs
DESC Number of Pre-allocated Read Data Buffers
PAR RNID_NUM_PREALLOC_BUF_PARAM
F 12 1 pab_en
DESC PUB AUB bridge enable 1'b1: Enabled 1'b0: Not enabled
PAR RNI_PAB_EN_PARAM
F 13 8 pab_logicalid
DESC PUB AUB bridge Logical ID
PAR RNI_PAB_LOGICALID_PARAM
F 21 1 ax_loopback_en
DESC LoopBack enable on ACE-Lite/AXI4 interface 1'b1: Enabled 1'b0: Not enabled
PAR RNID_AXLOOPBACK_EN_PARAM
F 22 1 ax_mpam_en
DESC MPAM enable on ACE-Lite/AXI4 interface 1'b1: Enabled 1'b0: Not enabled
PAR RNID_AXMPAM_EN_PARAM
R 0x980 64 - S por_rnd_secure_register_groups_override
RESET 0x0 0xf
DESC Allows non-secure access to predefined groups of secure registers.
F 0 1 cfg_ctl
DESC Allows non-secure access to secure configuration control register
F 1 1 port_ctrl
DESC Allows non-secure access to secure AXI port control registers
F 2 1 mpam_ctrl
DESC Allows non-secure access to secure AXI port MPAM override register
F 3 1 qos_ctrl
DESC Allows non-secure access to secure QoS control registers
R 0xa00 64 - S por_rnd_cfg_ctl
RESET 0x200201c41 0x47ff3ff7fff
DESC Functions as the configuration control register. Specifies the current mode.
SGO por_rnd_secure_register_groups_override.cfg_ctl
F 0 1 qpc_en
DESC When set, enables QPC-based scheduling using two QoS priority classes (QoS15 and non-QoS15)
F 1 1 wfc
DESC When set, enables waiting for completion (COMP) before dispatching dependent transaction (TXN)
F 2 1 dis_wr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered writes when set
F 3 1 force_prealloc_rdb
DESC When set, all reads from the RN-D are sent with a preallocated read data buffer
PAR RNID_FORCE_RDB_PREALLOC_PARAM
F 4 1 qpc15_entry_rsv_en
DESC Enables QPC15 entry reservation 1'b1: Reserves tracker entry for QoS15 requests 1'b0: Does not reserve tracker entry for QoS15 requests NOTE: Only valid and applicable when por_rnd_qpc_en is set
F 5 1 pcie_mstr_present
DESC Indicates PCIe master is present; must be set if PCIe master is present upstream of RN-I or RN-D
F 6 1 dis_port_token
DESC If set, disables per port reservation in the tracker(rd and wr)
F 7 1 dis_tunneled_req_throttling
DESC Disables retry based throttling of tunneled write requests
F 8 3 rrt_crdgnt_weight
DESC Determines weight of credit grant allocated to retried reads in presence of pending retried writes
F 11 1 rdata_64byt_nointv_en
DESC Enables no interleaving property on normal memory read data within 64B granule when set
F 12 3 wrt_crdgnt_weight
DESC Determines weight of credit grant allocated to retried writes in presence of pending retried reads
F 16 10 max_rrt_outstd_chitxn_cnt
DESC Maximum number of outstanding reads allowed on CHI-side
PAR RNID_NUM_RD_REQ_PARAM
F 28 10 max_wrt_outstd_chitxn_cnt
DESC Maximum number of outstanding writes allowed on CHI-side
PAR RNID_NUM_WR_REQ_PARAM
F 38 1 dis_awid_to_hni_hnp_cxra
DESC If set, disables compressed AWID to HNI and CXRA, also disables compressed AWID based ordering. Set this bit if uniq-ID write performance is needed.
F 42 1 en_subcacheline_rdonce_conv_to_cxra
DESC If set, enables the conversion of sub-cacheline RdOnce to RdNoSnp for CXRA targets
R 0xa08 64 - S por_rnd_aux_ctl
RESET 0x4012 0x3fdfff7
DESC Functions as the auxiliary control register for RN-D.
F 0 1 cg_disable
DESC Disables clock gating when set
F 1 1 ar_byp_en
DESC AR bypass enable; enables bypass path in the AR pipeline
F 2 1 park_port_arb_ptr
DESC Parks the AXI port arbitration pointer for Burst
F 4 1 upstrm_datcheck_en
DESC Upstream supports Datacheck
PAR POR_DATACHECK_EN_PARAM
F 5 1 dis_stash_wr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered WrUniqStash when set
F 6 1 dis_hni_wr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered writes to HNI when set
F 7 1 dis_pci_cxra_wr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered writes to PCI-CXRA when set
F 8 1 dis_misc_wr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered writes with following attributes when set : Device memory or EWA=0 or Excl=1
F 9 1 en_wrstream_data_dispatch_on_prior_completions
DESC If set, data dispatch for streaming writes waits for completion of all older writes
F 10 1 dis_wr_stream_on_tgttype_mismatch
DESC If set, serializes first write when moving from one tgttype to another
F 11 1 never_send_wr_full_op
DESC If set, RNI will never send WR FULL op. All write ops will be of PTL type
F 12 1 dis_tnl_burst_early_dealloc_opt
DESC If set, disables the optimization related to early deallocation of tunnelled writes for intermediate txns of burst
F 13 1 dis_data_chunking
DESC If set, disables the data chunking feature
F 14 1 dis_compack_on_writes
DESC If set, disables comp_ack on streaming writes. WrData is used for ordering writes
F 15 1 dis_rreq_bypass
DESC If set, disables read request bypass path
F 16 1 dis_rdata_bypass
DESC If set, disables read data bypass path; if rxdat_bp_en = 1'b0
F 18 1 rxdat_bp_en
DESC If set, back pressures the rxdat interface when RDB's are not available
F 19 1 dis_size_optimization_for_32B_incr
DESC If set, disables the size related optimization for a 32B INCR burst (rh-2512)
F 20 1 dis_hnp_wr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered writes to HNP when set
F 21 1 dis_pci_cxra_rd_burst
DESC If set, disables read burst to PCI-CXRA on CHI request flits . Read burst on CHI is supported only in non-decoupled RDB configuration.
F 22 1 dis_hnp_rd_burst
DESC If set, disables read burst to HNP on CHI request flits . Read burst on CHI is supported only in non-decoupled RDB configuration.
F 23 1 dis_subcacheline_rdonce_conv
DESC If set, disables the conversion of sub-cacheline RdOnce to RdNoSnp across all targets
F 24 1 dis_be_all_ones_hint
DESC If set, disables hint to HNF which signals all BE=1's on writes
F 25 1 dis_ncwr_stream
DESC Disables streaming of ordered non-cacheable writes when set
R 0xa10 64 - S por_rnd_s0_port_control
RESET 0x0 0xfffffff
DESC Controls port S0 AXI/ACE slave interface settings.
SGO por_rnd_secure_register_groups_override.port_ctrl
F 0 11 s0_lpid_mask
DESC Port S0 LPID mask LPID[0]: Equal to the result of UnaryOR of BitwiseAND of LPID mask and AXID (LPID[0] = |(AXID & mask)); specifies which AXID bit is reflected in the LSB of LPID LPID[2:1]: Equal to port ID[1:0]; the MSB of LPID contains port ID
F 11 7 s0_rd_token
DESC Port S0 reserved token count for AR channel per slice This should be less than the number of Rd requests(RNID_NUM_RD_REQ_PARAM) per slice on AR achnnel
F 18 7 s0_wr_token
DESC Port S0 reserved token count for AW channel This must be less than the number of Wr requests(RNID_NUM_WR_REQ_PARAM) on AW achnnel
F 25 1 s0_dis_data_interleaving
DESC If set, disables read DATA interleaving on RDATAS0 channel. This applies only to RDATA generated as a response to requests on AR channel . This does not apply to RDATA generated as a response to Atomic request on AW channel. I.e. RDATA of an Atomic op, on AW channel, may interleave with RDATA of an AR channel request
F 26 1 s0_sends_ar_unq_id
DESC If set, indicates AR transactions on Port0 are always Unique ID. This bit for a port must be set to 1 to enable Read Burst on the CHI side of RND.
F 27 1 s0_tablewalk_mstr_present
DESC Must be set if translation table walk master present such as TCU or GIC
R 0xa18 64 - S por_rnd_s1_port_control
RESET 0x0 0xfffffff
DESC Controls port S1 AXI/ACE slave interface settings.
SGO por_rnd_secure_register_groups_override.port_ctrl
F 0 11 s1_lpid_mask
DESC Port S1 LPID mask LPID[0]: Equal to the result of UnaryOR of BitwiseAND of LPID mask and AXID (LPID[0] = |(AXID & mask)); specifies which AXID bit is reflected in the LSB of LPID LPID[2:1]: Equal to port ID[1:0]; the MSB of LPID contains port ID
F 11 7 s1_rd_token
DESC Port S1 reserved token count for AR channel per slice This should be less than the number of Rd requests(RNID_NUM_RD_REQ_PARAM) per slice on AR achnnel
F 18 7 s1_wr_token
DESC Port S1 reserved token count for AW channel This must be less than the number of Wr requests(RNID_NUM_WR_REQ_PARAM) on AW achnnel
F 25 1 s1_dis_data_interleaving
DESC If set, disables read DATA interleaving on RDATAS1 channel. This applies only to RDATA generated as a response to requests on AR channel . This does not apply to RDATA generated as a response to Atomic request on AW channel. I.e. RDATA of an Atomic op, on AW channel, may interleave with RDATA of an AR channel request
F 26 1 s1_sends_ar_unq_id
DESC If set, indicates AR transactions on Port1 are always Unique ID. This bit for a port must be set to 1 to enable Read Burst on the CHI side of RND.
F 27 1 s1_tablewalk_mstr_present
DESC Must be set if translation table walk master present such as TCU or GIC
R 0xa20 64 - S por_rnd_s2_port_control
RESET 0x0 0xfffffff
DESC Controls port S2 AXI/ACE slave interface settings.
SGO por_rnd_secure_register_groups_override.port_ctrl
F 0 11 s2_lpid_mask
DESC Port S2 LPID mask LPID[0]: Equal to the result of UnaryOR of BitwiseAND of LPID mask and AXID (LPID[0] = |(AXID & mask)); specifies which AXID bit is reflected in the LSB of LPID LPID[2:1]: Equal to port ID[1:0]; the MSB of LPID contains port ID
F 11 7 s2_rd_token
DESC Port S2 reserved token count for AR channel per slice This should be less than the number of Rd requests(RNID_NUM_RD_REQ_PARAM) per slice on AR achnnel
F 18 7 s2_wr_token
DESC Port S2 reserved token count for AW channel This must be less than the number of Wr requests(RNID_NUM_WR_REQ_PARAM) on AW achnnel
F 25 1 s2_dis_data_interleaving
DESC If set, disables read DATA interleaving on RDATAS2 channel. This applies only to RDATA generated as a response to requests on AR channel . This does not apply to RDATA generated as a response to Atomic request on AW channel. I.e. RDATA of an Atomic op, on AW channel, may interleave with RDATA of an AR channel request
F 26 1 s2_sends_ar_unq_id
DESC If set, indicates AR transactions on Port2 are always Unique ID. This bit for a port must be set to 1 to enable Read Burst on the CHI side of RND.
F 27 1 s2_tablewalk_mstr_present
DESC Must be set if translation table walk master present such as TCU or GIC
R 0xa28 64 - S por_rnd_s0_mpam_control
RESET 0x0 0x101ff11
